    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113022,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113023,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E90.6 Benign neoplasm of nasopharynx</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113024,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> congenital pleomorphic adenoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113025,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113026,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Salivary gland anlage tumours occur in the posterior nasal septum or posterior nasopharyngeal wall.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113027,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with feeding difficulty and respiratory distress due to nasal airway obstruction {15656947}. Before birth, salivary gland anlage tumour may be associated with polyhydramnios {25149159}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113028,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "<p >Approximately 40&nbsp;examples of salivary gland anlage tumour have been reported {7402665; 8279626; 15656947; 19025657; 19112069; 19289716; 20704478; 21391752; 22896937; 25149159}. The affected patients are infants (diagnosed by 3&nbsp;months of age) and there is a male predilection. An in&nbsp;utero case has been reported {25149159}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-11T16:30:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113029,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113030,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Whole-exome sequencing of 3&nbsp;cases showed no plausible driver mutations {30598408}, suggestive of a possible hamartomatous origin for these tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113031,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Salivary gland anlage tumour is a polypoid to pedunculated, smooth, tan-brown mass with a solid to microcystic cut surface {15656947}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113032,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Salivary gland anlage tumour is characterized by a complex network of tubules and ducts. Submucosal ducts and solid and cystic squamous nests with variable keratinization are continuous with the surface squamous epithelium. The subepithelial stroma tends to be hypocellular, with more cellular stromal nodules in the centre of the polyp. Cellular atypia and mitoses are absent {15656947}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The myoepithelial nature of the stromal cells is confirmed by positive immunohistochemistry for cytokeratins and SMA.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113033,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "<p >Cytological examination is rarely required, but if done, it may reveal cohesive tissue fragments (some with duct-like structures) of uniform cells with small oval nuclei, inconspicuous nucleoli, and sparse cytoplasm with indistinct borders. A component of metaplastic squamous epithelium may be present {9181318}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T12:28:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113034,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:48:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113035,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 75,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> a polypoid lesion with a complex network of ducts and solid-cystic squamous nests, showing continuity with surface squamous epithelium; hypocellular to cellular spindle cell stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> spindly cells positive for cytokeratins and SMA (in selected cases).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-11T16:30:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
